  "final_message": "I haven't made any changes. Removing `channel` from `OrderPlaced` conflicts with ARCH-4, so I want your decision first.\n\n**The conflict:** `OrderPlaced` (`src/core/events.ts:16`, schemaVersion 3) is consumed by billing-service and analytics-ingest, which are deployed from other repos. ARCH-4 says changes must be additive and removals must go through deprecation. \"This service no longer reads `channel`\" doesn't tell us whether those consumers read it. If either one does, dropping the field would break it in production.\n\n**Why I didn't do just the model part:** `order.channel` is what fills the event field (`events.ts:50`). Removing it from the order model also means changing the `POST /orders` input parsing (`requestParsing.ts`) and validation (`order.ts:124`). It would also change what the API accepts, so the two removals are coupled.\n\n**Options:**\n1. **Deprecate first (my recommendation).**\n   - Mark `channel` on `OrderPlaced` as `@deprecated`.\n   - Stop requiring it on input. Keep the order model optional or defaulted so the event still carries a value.\n   - Remove it once billing-service and analytics-ingest confirm they don't read it, probably with a schemaVersion bump.\n2. **Remove it everywhere now.** Do this only if you can confirm both consumers are fine without it, or if Architecture has signed off on the breaking change. Tell me that and I'll make the change. It touches the model, event, request parsing, validation, the README and CLAUDE.md examples, and several tests.\n3. **Remove it from the order model and API only.** The event would keep `channel`, but it would need some other source for the value, such as a constant. That seems to defeat the purpose.\n\nWhich of these do you want?",
